feat: upload-first auto-extraction UX with vision guardrails

Replace the manual JSON-entry workflow with a drag-and-drop card that
classifies the document, extracts fields, and surfaces confidence so
users only edit when the model is uncertain.

Backend
- extraction.py: new strict envelope {doc_type, doc_type_confidence,
  quality, patient_name, fields, warnings}; _coerce_envelope validates
  doc_type against DocumentType enum, clamps confidence, normalises
  quality, and forces UNREADABLE when the model returns UNKNOWN with no
  fields. _failed_envelope returns a canonical shape on LLM/network
  errors so the frontend can always render.
- main.py: /api/upload no longer requires actual_type; honours user
  override when supplied; returns confidence, warnings, extraction_status
  and a needs_review flag (true when status != OK, quality != GOOD,
  confidence < 0.7, or type == UNKNOWN).

Frontend
- api.ts: UploadResult type with the new fields; api.upload() now takes
  an optional actualType.
- ClaimForm.tsx: replace DocumentUploader with DocumentCard, a 4-state
  component (idle / uploading / extracted / error). Idle shows a big
  drop-zone; extracted shows a compact preview (type pill, colour-coded
  quality, confidence, patient, field count) plus a warnings banner; the
  manual editor stays available behind an "Edit details" expander and
  auto-opens whenever needs_review is true.
